        />
    </p>
        <p>
        The Power Mac G4 Cube came as a surprise after much conflicting behind-the-scenes information. Like the iMac, It was a silent machine with no fan. Steve Jobs presented the Cube with the words: “The G4 Cube is simply the coolest computer ever. An entirely new class of computer, it marries the Pentium-crushing performance of the Power Mac G4 with the miniaturization, silent operation and elegant desktop design of the iMac. It is an amazing engineering and design feat, and we’re thrilled to finally unveil it to our customers.”
The model failed, however, largely due to the price. The first version was also prone to frequent overheating and sometimes closed down spontaneously; the plastic casing also tended to crack. Apple’s share price fell as a result; a trend only reversed with the unveiling of the first iPod.
Apple&#039;s idea of a small desktop computer wasn‘t rejected outright however, and the company tried to conquer the market with the Mac Mini. It was probably another case of the market not being quite ready for such an innovation.
    </p>
